---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageNav from "@/components/layout/PageNav.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/layout/Footer.astro";
import galleryAbout from "@/assets/heroes/galleryabout.webp";

import BeatifulBeachBali from "@/assets/heroes/BeatifulBeachBali.jpg";
---

<Layout
  title="About — Voyaflair"
  description="Meet Joanna, creator of Voyaflair — a personal travel journal sharing destinations, stays, and experiences worth remembering."
>
  <PageNav />

  <header
    class="flex flex-col relative items-center justify-center max-w-none min-h-[600px] w-auto mx-0 px-1.5"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center h-full w-full gap-[30px]">
      <h1>My Little Story</h1>
      <p
        class="max-w-[70ch] leading-[1.5] text-[clamp(1.125rem,4.2vw,1.5rem)] text-center"
      >
        Hi, I’m Joanna — originally from Greece and now based in
        Oslo.
      </p>
      <p
        class="max-w-[70ch] w-full leading-[1.5] text-[clamp(1.125rem,4.2vw,1.5rem)] text-center"
      >
        I started traveling abroad almost ten years ago, and since then, travel
        has become a big part of my life. I’ve been fortunate enough to visit
        more than 20 countries — and I’ve returned to many of them more than
        once.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="relative min-h-[500px] w-full p-4 box-border z-0">
    <div
      class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row items-center justify-center lg:items-start lg:justify-center w-full gap-10 overflow-visible parallax-layers"
    >
      <div
        class="h-[50svh] max-w-full w-full lg:max-w-[560px] md:h-[512px] md:max-w-[520px] back overflow-hidden md:flex-1"
      >
        <Image
          class="block h-full w-full bg-[#e8e8e8] object-cover white-placeholder"
          src={BeatifulBeachBali}
          alt="Beautiful beach in Bali"
          widths={[400, 800, 1120]}
          sizes="(max-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 32px), 560px"
        />
      </div>
      <div
        class="flex items-center justify-center md:items-start md:justify-start max-w-full w-full lg:max-w-[560px] md:h-[612px] md:max-w-[520px] box-border cinematic-copy md:flex-1"
      >
        <blockquote class="flex flex-col w-full py-4">
          <p class="leading-[1.5] text-[clamp(1.125rem,4.2vw,1.5rem)]">
            While I love discovering new places, I also enjoy returning to
            destinations I already love. There is always something new to
            discover — a different neighborhood, a hidden café, a local
            experience I missed the first time, or simply a new way of seeing a
            familiar place.
          </p>
          <p
            class="pt-8 leading-[1.5] text-[clamp(1.125rem,4.2vw,1.5rem)] text-start"
          >
            And if you’re wondering what makes a destination one of my
            favorites, it’s never just one thing. It’s the combination of many
            things: the food, the atmosphere, the people you meet, the
            adventures you have, and all those small moments that stay with you
            long after you return home.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="relative mb-16 px-4 lg:px-24 md:mt-10 md:mx-auto container-3 z-10">
    <p
      class="w-full leading-snug text-[clamp(1.125rem,4.2vw,1.5rem)] text-start lg:text-[1.35rem] md:text-[1.25rem] scaleUp-3"
      data-scale-from="0.6"
    >
      Long before I began sharing my travels online, I was the person who would
      spend hours researching destinations, comparing places to stay, saving
      beautiful cafés and restaurants, and putting together detailed
      itineraries. I genuinely enjoyed the planning process almost as much as
      the trip itself. After every trip, friends would often ask me about my
      experiences: Which places did I love? Where should they stay? What was
      worth adding to their itinerary? What would I do differently next time?
      Over time, I realized that all the research and planning I enjoyed so much
      could also be useful to other people.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section
    class="container grid relative items-center min-h-screen w-full gap-6 p-4 lg:gap-12 md:p-8 grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center w-full md:h-[600px] py-6 md:py-12">
      <blockquote
        class="flex flex-col justify-center h-full space-y-4 leading-[1.5] text-[clamp(1.25rem,3.5vw,1.5rem)] scaleUp"
        data-scale-from="0.6"
      >
        <p
          class="leading-[1.5] text-[clamp(1.125rem,4.2vw,1.5rem)] tracking-tight"
        >
          So, years later, I created my Instagram account as a place to share
          beautiful destinations that I genuinely believe are worth
          experiencing, along with practical travel tips — especially the kind
          of advice I wish someone had given me before some of my own trips.
        </p>
        <p
          class="leading-[1.5] text-[clamp(1.125rem,4.2vw,1.5rem)] tracking-tight"
        >
          But there was always more I wanted to share than could fit into a
          post. More details, more recommendations, more context, and, of
          course, complete itineraries that could help make travel planning feel
          a little easier. That’s how this blog began.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div
      class="h-[300px] w-full md:h-[600px] container-title overflow-hidden"
    >
      <Image
        class="h-full w-full bg-[#e8e8e8] object-cover"
        data-scale-from="0.6"
        src={galleryAbout}
        alt="Beautiful beach in Bali"
        widths={[400, 800, 1120]}
        sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="relative mb-16 px-4 lg:px-24 md:mt-10 md:mx-auto container-last z-10"
  >
    <p
      class="w-full leading-snug text-[clamp(1.125rem,4.2vw,1.5rem)] sm:text-start md:text-center lg:text-[1.35rem] md:text-[1.25rem] container-title"
      data-scale-from="0.6"
    >
      This is where I share carefully chosen destinations, meaningful stays,
      memorable experiences, useful travel tips, and thoughtfully planned
      itineraries. Some guides are here to help you plan a trip from start to
      finish; others are simply meant to inspire your next journey. My hope is
      that Voyaflair can save you some time, help you discover places you might
      not have found otherwise, and make planning your trip feel more enjoyable
      — leaving you with a little more time to look forward to the journey… and
      pack your suitcase.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Footer />

  <script>
    import gsap from "gsap";
    import { ScrollTrigger } from "gsap/ScrollTrigger";

    gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);
    (gsap.utils.toArray("[data-scale-from]") as HTMLElement[]).forEach((el) => {
      gsap.fromTo(
        el,
        {
          scale: Number(el.dataset.scaleFrom) || 0.6,
          transformOrigin: "top center",
        },
        {
          scale: 1,
          ease: "none",
          scrollTrigger: {
            trigger: el.parentElement,
            start: "top bottom",
            end: "center center",
            scrub: 1,
          },
        },
      );
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
